   "snippet": "Expected after India’s Ladakh naming, the FM’s trade-barrier callouts & tighter FDI PN3 scrutiny for China.\n\nChinese are posturing. Beijing rarely imposes permanent bans; expect waivers. Licensing bottlenecks create uncertain lead times for Indian EPC contractors pricing Chinese equip—next 'case-by-case' waivers may force contractors to disclose precise project locations & site data to MOFCOM to prove \"non-military\" use.\n\nBottomline: suit up & invest—or suck up and stop the border posturing without sufficient leverage.",
