   "title": "Like with Russia, Trump will fail with Myanmar.",
   "url": "https://x.com/Neuro24de/status/2111836680864800993",
   "snippet": "Like with Russia, Trump will fail with Myanmar. China is already there and will be the main trading partner in the next decade. What ever Trump wants to extract from Myanmar, will need Chinas approval. \nRelations between Myanmar and China are close and shaped by strategic, economic, and geopolitical self-interest. China is Myanmar’s most important trading partner, primary source of imports, and largest investor. Bilateral trade volume stood at approximately $19.4 billion in 2025 (a 19.1% increase from the previous year). As part of China’s “New Silk Road” (Belt and Road Initiative), Beijing is expanding the economic corridor to gain direct land and infrastructure access to the Indian Ocean via Myanmar. China exports vehicles and electromechanical equipment to Myanmar and, in return, imports mineral resources (such as rare earths and mining products) as well as agricultural goods",
   "body": "Like with Russia, Trump will fail with Myanmar. China is already there and will be the main trading partner in the next decade. What ever Trump wants to extract from Myanmar, will need Chinas approval. \nRelations between Myanmar and China are close and shaped by strategic, economic, and geopolitical self-interest. China is Myanmar’s most important trading partner, primary source of imports, and largest investor. Bilateral trade volume stood at approximately $19.4 billion in 2025 (a 19.1% increase from the previous year). As part of China’s “New Silk Road” (Belt and Road Initiative), Beijing is expanding the economic corridor to gain direct land and infrastructure access to the Indian Ocean via Myanmar. China exports vehicles and electromechanical equipment to Myanmar and, in return, imports mineral resources (such as rare earths and mining products) as well as agricultural goods",
